# fluid2d.numos — Fluid 2D (APP 14) screenshot script for the marketing site.
#
# Website deliverables (source of truth: paadweb/public/apps/index.html,
# transcribed in DELIVERABLES.md and tests/emulator/scripts/screenshots/README.md):
#   1. /assets/img/apps/fluid-1.webp  ->  out/shots-fluid2d-1.ppm
#      SHOW: wind tunnel preset, VELOCITY palette, flow entering from the
#      left and wrapping around the obstacle in a coloured wake.
#      CAPTION: Flow around an obstacle, coloured by speed and direction.
#   2. /assets/img/apps/fluid-2.webp  ->  out/shots-fluid2d-2.ppm
#      SHOW: convection preset, THERMAL palette, plumes rising from the
#      heated floor, curling over and sinking down the sides.
#      CAPTION: Heat driven convection, with nobody touching the controls.
#   3. /assets/img/apps/fluid-3.webp  ->  out/shots-fluid2d-3.ppm
#      SHOW: two dyes in one velocity field — red from the left, blue from
#      the right — meeting in the middle and mixing into a band of purple.
#      CAPTION: Two dyes, one flow, mixing where they collide.
#
# ── BLOCKER: Fluid 2D cannot run in the PC emulator ──────────────────
# Proven three independent ways:
#   1. ROUTING. The emulator runs its own dispatch in src/hal/NativeHal.cpp
#      (not src/SystemApp.cpp). Its launchApp() has cases 0-7, 10, 18
#      (opt-in), 20, 21, 22, 23 and APPID_MATH_SHOWCASE — but NO case 14.
#      ENTER on the Fluid 2D card prints "[APP] App 14 no implementada en
#      simulador" and the context stays MENU (verified by running this
#      script: the post-launch assert_app Menu below PASSES).
#   2. IDENTITY. The emulator's AppMode enum (NativeHal.cpp:272) and the
#      shared numos::Ctx enum (src/ui/AppContext.h — the public @ctx
#      contract, "append only") have no fluid entry. canonicalAppName() /
#      scriptAppNameToId() do not know "fluid2d", so `open_app fluid2d`
#      and `assert_app Fluid2D` are parse errors (exit 2). Only
#      assert_menu_focus resolves the card (it reads the real APPS[] table).
#   3. BINARY. The prebuilt emulator (C:/.piobuild/numOS/emulator_pc/program,
#      newer than every source file) contains zero Fluid2DApp symbols
#      (nm) and none of Fluid2DApp.cpp's distinctive strings ("Re:%.0f",
#      "F2D0"): Fluid2DApp.cpp is firmware-only (ESP32 target) and is not
#      compiled into the PC build. The app's state machines can never run
#      here, so no honest fluid frame can exist.
#
# Because of that, this script deliberately contains NO screenshot lines:
# a frame of the launcher written to out/shots-fluid2d-N.ppm would be a
# picture of the wrong screen shipped to the website. All three shots are
# reported as COULD NOT CAPTURE.
#
# ── Per-shot state machines (traced from Fluid2DApp::handleKey, ──────
#    src/apps/Fluid2DApp.cpp:277 — ready to enable if the emulator ever
#    gains a launchApp case 14 with Fluid2DApp in the PC build) ────────
#    SHOT 1: key f5        # FlowPreset NONE -> WIND_TUNNEL (fields reset;
#                          # obstacle block at x 19..23, y 21..27 via
#                          # setupWindTunnel(); every 30 Hz tick
#                          # applyFlowPresetForces() adds vx=+80 and
#                          # dens+=10 at column 1: flow from the left)
#            key f2        # Palette CLASSIC -> THERMAL
#            key f2        # Palette THERMAL -> VELOCITY (velocityToColor:
#                          # hue = flow direction, value = speed)
#            wait 300      # sim ticks at ~30 Hz (33 ms lv_timer); the
#                          # wake behind the obstacle needs time to form
#    SHOT 2: key f5        # WIND_TUNNEL -> CONVECTION_CELL (fields reset,
#                          # no obstacles; floor heating: temp+=200 at
#                          # bottom centre, temp-=50 at top, dens+=20;
#                          # applyBuoyancy() drives the plumes upward)
#            key f2 x3     # VELOCITY -> MIXED -> CLASSIC -> THERMAL
#                          # (inferno LUT for the temperature field)
#            wait 600      # plumes need time to rise, curl over and sink
#    SHOT 3: key f5        # CONVECTION_CELL -> NONE (fields reset)
#            key f2 x2     # THERMAL -> VELOCITY -> MIXED (mixedColor():
#                          # densA -> red, densB -> blue, overlap -> purple)
#            key left x22  # cursor from centre (32,24) to (10,24)
#            key exe x3    # RED_INK brush: radial high-pressure burst —
#                          # red dye + momentum, expands rightward
#            key right x44 # cursor to (54,24)
#            key f1        # brush RED_INK -> BLUE_INK
#            key exe x3    # blue burst from the right, expands leftward;
#                          # the two fronts collide and mix mid-field
#            wait 200
#
# Run (repo root):
#   ./"C:/.piobuild/numOS/emulator_pc/program" --headless --deterministic \
#       --script tests/emulator/scripts/screenshots/fluid2d.numos \
#       --fs-root tests/emulator/fs --frames 1400 --quiet
#
# Exit codes: 0 ok · 2 script/parse error · 3 screenshot write error · 4 assertion failure.

log "fluid2d: waiting for launcher"
wait 200
assert_app Menu
assert_theme numos

# Navigate the numos 3-column launcher grid to the Fluid 2D card.
# Grid layout (menu_nav_parity.numos): row 4 = Bridge(12), Circuit(13),
# Fluid 2D(14). Focus starts on Calculation (row 0, col 0):
# DOWN x4 -> row 4 col 0 (Bridge), RIGHT x2 -> row 4 col 2 (Fluid 2D).
key down
wait 10
key down
wait 10
key down
wait 10
key down
wait 10
key right
wait 10
key right
wait 10

# Strongest true claim the emulator can make about this app: the Fluid 2D
# launcher card exists at id 14 and is focused. (assert_app Fluid2D is not
# even parseable — canonicalAppName() has no "fluid2d" entry.)
assert_menu_focus fluid2d

# Attempt the launch the way a user would: ENTER on the focused card.
key enter
wait 150

# launchApp(14) is unimplemented in the emulator, so the context is still
# MENU: Fluid2DApp never became active, no solver tick ever ran, and none
# of the fluid state above (presets, palettes, dyes) can exist. Asserting
# Menu here is the proof that the capture is impossible, not an oversight.
assert_app Menu
assert_theme numos

# No screenshot lines on purpose — see BLOCKER above. The three website
# shots are COULD NOT CAPTURE: the app is not wired into the PC emulator.

log "fluid2d: done — Fluid 2D (app 14) is not launchable in the PC emulator (launchApp has no case 14); no honest capture exists"
